1. I have found a fountain of life, a fresh living spring flowing from heaven above;
Free from earthly struggles and entanglements, joyfully drinking from the "Elim" spring of love.
What a holy, heavenly living spring, flowing continually deep within me;
Bringing joy and satisfaction, ever increasing, no human words can fully express.
(Chorus)
Come and drink freely from the fountain of living water, without cost, if only you are willing;
The living water's supply is sweet, rich, and infinite, for the Lord Himself is this fountain.

2. I now take refuge in the fountain that washes away sin, cleansing all filth and guilt;
Through the Lord's precious blood my sins are forgiven, white as snow I stand before God.
Justified by God not by my merits, but because Christ lives in me;
I partake of the heavenly nature without ceasing, in Him I am made complete.
(Chorus)
Come and drink freely from the fountain of living water, without cost, if only you are willing;
The living water's supply is sweet, rich, and infinite, for the Lord Himself is this fountain.

3. The gracious Lord is also my fountain of healing, my secret supply without limit;
Far beyond human wisdom's reach and sight, and not redeemable by wealth.
This healing living spring is holy and perfect, flowing from the pierced side of the Savior;
By His stripes I am healed, and He comes to make His home in my heart.
(Chorus)
Come and drink freely from the fountain of living water, without cost, if only you are willing;
The living water's supply is sweet, rich, and infinite, for the Lord Himself is this fountain.

4. I love to drink from the fountain of joy, as my strength overflowing in my heart;
The Lord is my sunlight, brilliant and radiant, my rejoicing is in Him.
The glory of grass and flowers withers in a moment, human feasts are brief as clouds and smoke;
The Lord is my joy, never diminishing, delighting in God on earth as in heaven.
(Chorus)
Come and drink freely from the fountain of living water, without cost, if only you are willing;
The living water's supply is sweet, rich, and infinite, for the Lord Himself is this fountain.
